        G


    {\displaystyle G}

 on a set 



        S


    {\displaystyle S}

 is, loosely speaking, an operation that takes an element of 



        G


    {\displaystyle G}

 and an element of 



        S


    {\displaystyle S}

 and produces another element of 



        S
        .


    {\displaystyle S.}

  More formally, it is a group homomorphism from 



        G


    {\displaystyle G}

 to the automorphism group of 



        S


    {\displaystyle S}

 (the set of all bijections on 



        S


    {\displaystyle S}

 along with group operation being function composition). One says that 



        G


    {\displaystyle G}

 acts on 



        S
        .


